## Objective
- Perform the round-1 adversarial review of phase-097 (`time.parse`/date formatting) in the redblue checkout and output exactly one `FINDINGS:` list plus a mandatory final `REVIEW VERDICT:` line.

## Important Details
- Reviewer is READ-ONLY; available tools are `glob`, `grep`, `read` only. `bash` is unavailable and `external_directory` access is denied, so no tests can be run and chrono source cannot be read.
- Contract requires: every finding cites `file:line` actually read; severities are exactly `BLOCKER`, `MAJOR`, `MINOR`, `STYLE`; a `BLOCKER` must carry `VERIFIED: <how>` or be downgraded to `MAJOR`; final line must be `REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS <count>` or `REVIEW VERDICT: CLEAN`; if no findings, output exactly `FINDINGS: none`.
- The phase is claimed gate-green: `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy -D warnings`, `cargo test --all-targets` (2283 passed), `../rbops/verify.sh phase-097`.
- Change set: committed `04fa334..HEAD` (large `src/runtime.rs` +509/−43, `src/value.rs` +13/−1, `src/stdlib.rs` +9/−2, SPEC/README/SURVEY/REPORT, many tests) plus uncommitted work adding a caller-chosen layout parser (`src/runtime.rs` +54/−3, `src/stdlib.rs` +1/−1, `tests/time_builtin_test.rs` +81, `tests/doc_blocks_runs.txt` +2/−2, README/SPEC/REPORT).
- chrono version is `0.4.45` (`Cargo.lock:82-83`).
- Existing tests pin ISO-form behavior: `tests/time_builtin_test.rs:907` (`edge_time_parse_refuses_an_offset_that_moves_an_edge_date_out_of_range`) and `:909-910` (edge dates `-262143-01-01`, `262142-12-31`). The test at `:1221` (`edge_time_parse_names_the_year_when_the_calendar_cannot_hold_it`, input `262143-01-01`) is not listed in REPORT's test table; its validity depends on chrono's max year (262142 vs 262143) and cannot be checked without running.
- New layout tests: `tests/time_builtin_test.rs:1429` (`edge_time_parse_reads_a_callers_layout`), `:1455` (`edge_time_parse_layout_refuses_bad_text_and_bad_layout`), `:1487` (`edge_time_parse_layout_agrees_across_engines`). No test covers a zone-bearing layout (`%z`/`%Z`) whose `DateTime` conversion fails, nor `%Z` zone names.

## Work State
### Completed
- Read `src/runtime.rs` time code: `seconds_for_instant` (`:559`), `parse_iso8601` (`:725`), `parse_legacy_unix_text` (`:948`), `parse_with_layout` (`:964-981`), `unix_seconds_for` (`:1032`), `expect_date` (`:1203`), dispatch for `time_format`/`time_parse`/`time_unix`/`time_from_unix` (`~:1750-1880`).
- Read `src/value.rs` (`Date(NaiveDateTime)` at `:265`, `date_text` at `:332`), `src/stdlib.rs` registration (`:443-473`), `BUILTIN_NAMES` (`:1165`, closes `input` at `:1250`), signatures (`:1389-1398`), `MODULE_MEMBERS` (`:63`).
- Read SPEC time section (`SPEC.md:1408-1575`), README time block (`README.md:225-244`), SURVEY rank 6, phase REPORT, and time tests.
- Verified the shared `date_text` printer is used by JSON (`src/runtime.rs:1040`) and `to_text` goes through `Value::Display` (`src/runtime.rs:2117-2127`).

### Active
- Candidate finding (likely `MAJOR`): `parse_with_layout` at `src/runtime.rs:964-981` falls through from `chrono::DateTime::parse_from_str` to `NaiveDateTime::parse_from_str`. Chrono's `NaiveDateTime` parser accepts and **ignores** an offset/zone in the layout, so a zone-bearing layout can silently return the local wall time instead of applying the offset or refusing. The doc comment at `:959-963` falsely claims “only `NaiveDateTime` reads a clock time without one.”
  - Repro to cite: `time.parse("262142-12-31T23:59:59-01:00", "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z")` — the ISO form refuses this at `tests/time_builtin_test.rs:907` because applying `-01:00` leaves the calendar; the layout form falls back to `NaiveDateTime` and returns `262142-12-31 23:59:59`, silently dropping the offset.
  - `%Z` repro: `time.parse("2024-01-01 12:00:00 EST", "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z")` is silently treated as UTC because `DateTime::parse_from_str` cannot resolve a zone name and the fallback ignores it.
  - Fix direction: only fall back to `NaiveDateTime` when the layout has no offset/zone item, or reject when a zone-bearing layout fails `DateTime`.
- Secondary candidate (`MINOR`): `parse_with_layout`’s unreadable-layout error (`src/runtime.rs` around `:966-970`) names the builtin and layout but not the text, while `SPEC.md:1560-1563` says layout errors name “the builtin, the text and the layout.”
- Unverified/speculative: possible chrono max-year mismatch at `tests/time_builtin_test.rs:1221`; leap-second date produced by layout form (`%S` = `:60`) may break `to_text`→`time.parse` round-trip and `time.unix` consistency. Do not report as BLOCKER without verification.

### Blocked
- Cannot run `cargo test`/probe programs or read chrono source (read-only tools; external directories denied). Any BLOCKER-level claim requiring execution must be downgraded or explicitly noted as unverified.

## Next Move
1. Finish the review and output the exact required format: numbered findings with `file:line`, severity, explanation, concrete fix, then the final `REVIEW VERDICT:` line.
2. Likely report the `parse_with_layout` offset/zone fallback as `MAJOR` (cite `src/runtime.rs:964-981`, `:959-963`, `tests/time_builtin_test.rs:907`), optionally the error-message omission as `MINOR`, and avoid speculative year/leap-second claims.

