1. [MINOR] `src/runtime.rs:965-969` — The unreadable-layout refusal omits the timestamp, but `SPEC.md:1560-1563` says every layout error names "the builtin, the text and the layout." `time.parse("2024-01-01", "%Q")` reports only `time.parse does not understand the format "%Q"`. The test at `tests/time_builtin_test.rs:1460-1463` checks only the layout phrase, so it cannot catch the omission. Fix: include the text in the message, e.g. `"{builtin} does not understand the format {format:?} for {text:?}"`.

2. [MINOR] `src/runtime.rs:955-956,971-979` — The comment advertises `%Z` as a supported zone, but a `%Z` name carries no offset: `DateTime::parse_from_str` cannot produce an instant from it, so the `NaiveDateTime` fallback reads the wall time as UTC. `time.parse("2024-01-01 12:00:00 EST", "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z")` therefore does not mean 17:00 UTC (and if chrono refuses the name, the documented support is still absent). Zone abbreviations are ambiguous, so reject `%Z` or accept only UTC/GMT, and align `SPEC.md:1558-1560` and the comment.

3. [MINOR] `src/runtime.rs:971-979` — The layout form cannot read the expanded year `time.format` writes. `time.format(time.parse("+10000-01-01"), "%Y-%m-%d")` writes `+10000-01-01`, but `time.parse("+10000-01-01", "%Y-%m-%d")` goes through chrono's `%Y`, which rejects years above 9999 (`phases/phase-035/FINDINGS.md:81`), so the layout round trip fails at the window's last instant. The one-argument form handles it (`tests/time_builtin_test.rs:1172-1178`); the layout form does not. Fix: special-case expanded years in the layout path or document the limit.

